[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8c881975-e340-5cbe-af54-e24457b3b1ee",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=5 \\\\ -x-y+4z &=-4 \\\\ -x-4y-6z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -6 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -6 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -6 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -7 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "312f90a2-36ca-515a-a9f1-906f58769e05",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
