  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0c32b465-a784-51f0-ac5e-b94f5d6ae7d6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z &=-4 \\\\ -x+4y &=2 \\\\ x-2y+4z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b8c49712-a418-5ac8-8cfe-bb99de241469",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
