    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "606a1393-efb7-5ef6-ad41-65b464ae3cc6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-2z &=-1 \\\\ 2x-5y-z &=0 \\\\ x-5y-10z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -10 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -10 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -10 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1d928c93-baad-50d9-bdee-8230fe6b0e3b",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
