    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0edb9d7f-d112-55b1-99e2-5e8ac295bc57",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+3z &=-1 \\\\ x+2y+2z &=-3 \\\\ x-y+5z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "4e58be76-c973-5cf1-bb1d-4452a76c8eab",
