  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "21aac157-f562-561d-97a7-548f8050de19",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-z &=4 \\\\ 2x-5y &=7 \\\\ 2x-5y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "41d8ac31-d8c3-5912-b361-f278774a117b",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
