    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "11be1b5a-0035-58b7-bd3a-f0787df2d0b1",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=-5 \\\\ 2x-y+6z &=-5 \\\\ -2x+3y-2z &=14\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2 & 14\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2 & 14\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-1,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d404ae5c-554e-5224-9d83-b018a3fe88ff",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
