    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d21c6cf2-57c0-5eb7-9274-416396a67dc3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-3z &=4 \\\\ -2x-3y+9z &=-3 \\\\ 2x+5y-3z &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -3 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -3 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -3 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-4,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
