    "question": {
      ":question/id": "79a03899-cbbd-538b-8820-144b5c5d7432",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z &=-5 \\\\ 2x+5y+2z &=-11 \\\\ x+3y-z &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & -9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & -9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 & -9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f8114461-582d-5277-aa0c-10606a624dee",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
